        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Epic of Gilgamesh</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1800 BCE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Made by</span><span class="info-stat-val">Mesopotamian scribes: five Sumerian poems about <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilgamesh">Gilgamesh</a>, some perhaps from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-dynasty-of-ur">Third Dynasty of Ur</a>; an Akkadian combined epic in its Old Babylonian version; and the Standard Babylonian version compiled from earlier texts by Sîn-lēqi-unninni, thought to have lived between 1300 and 1000 BCE.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Form</span><span class="info-stat-val">An epic poem in Akkadian, with Sumerian forerunners, written in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuneiform">cuneiform</a> on clay tablets; the Standard Babylonian version runs to twelve tablets, of which about two-thirds have been recovered, and uses much parallelism across two or three adjacent lines.</span></div>
